/** Command reference for the audit and canonical release workflow handoff. */
pub fn usage() -> string {
  return """
Usage:
  scripts/with_env.sh harn run --no-sandbox release_harn.harn -- --mode audit
  scripts/with_env.sh harn run --no-sandbox release_harn.harn -- --mock --agent --no-chat
  scripts/with_env.sh harn run --no-sandbox release_harn.harn -- --mode ship-pr --yes-live-release

Modes:
  audit    Inspect release readiness and write an audit report. Default.
  ship-pr  Dispatch Harn's no-input bump-release.yml on main and record its exact
           workflow handoff. Harn selects the version, opens the release PR,
           certifies its archives, and publishes after consumer qualification.
           Dispatch returns pending; it does not prove publication.

Local preparation, tagging, certification, and mock shipping are retired.
Live ship-pr rejects local source, version, planner, certification, and queue
overrides. Use watch_harn_release.harn with the returned receipt to observe
publication. The audit does not certify release readiness.

Audit flags:
  --repo PATH             Harn checkout. Defaults to ~/projects/harn.
  --base BRANCH           Release range base. Defaults to main.
  --at-sha SHA            Inspect this source commit instead of origin/<base>.
  --allow-base-drift      Allow a diagnostic pin whose base ancestry is unproven.
  --bump TYPE             patch, minor, major, premajor, preminor, prepatch, prerelease.
  --preid IDENTIFIER      Required for prerelease bumps; invalid for stable bumps.
  --expect-pr N           Require this PR in the selected range. Repeatable.
  --reject-pr N           Refuse this PR in the selected range. Repeatable.
  --bootstrap-new-crates  Include new workspace crate release metadata.
  --agent                Ask a model to review the measured audit evidence.
  --model MODEL           Override the configured planner model.
  --provider PROVIDER     Override the configured planner provider.
  --focus TEXT            Context for the review.
  --mock                  Use deterministic audit fixtures without API spend.
  --yes-live-release      Required for the live ship-pr handoff.

Audits use an isolated checkout and a process-owned workspace lease. If another
audit owns the reusable workspace, a per-run checkout preserves isolation.

Chat:
  Interactive terminals enter post-run chat unless HARN_EXT_CHAT=0.
  --no-chat               Skip all chat hooks, including in a terminal.
  --chat-only             Discuss a prior run without running the audit.
  --chat-run RUN_ID|DIR   Select its UUID, run directory, or release-audit.json.
  --chat-timeout-s N      Start-typing timeout in seconds. Defaults to 60.
  Post-run chat retains its existing repository inspection and repair tools.

Credentials:
  Harn reads provider keys from the environment. scripts/with_env.sh loads
  HARN_EXT_BUMP_FLEET_ENV_FILE (default ~/projects/burin-code/.env), then
  HARN_EXT_BUMP_FLEET_ENV_FILES, ./.env, and ./.env.local in override order.
  Live workflow handoff also requires the configured GitHub connector identity.
"""
}
